---
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const updated = "November 11, 2026";
const contact = "contact@androz2091.fr";
---

<Layout title="Pokercode bots: Privacy Policy">
	<div class="container mx-auto w-full px-4">
		<Navbar />
		<article class="max-w-3xl pb-16 space-y-4 leading-relaxed [&_h1]:text-4xl [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:pt-6 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:space-y-2 [&_a]:underline [&_code]:font-mono">
			<h1>Privacy Policy: Pokercode Discord bots</h1>
			<p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>

			<p>
				This policy covers the two Discord bots of the Pokercode community server:
				<strong>Pokercode</strong> (application ID 987333072250871878) and
				<strong>Pokercode Quiz</strong> (application ID 1014190706253910167).
				Both bots are built for the Pokercode Discord server and only process data from it.
				They are developed and operated by Simon Lefort (Androz2091) for Pokercode.
			</p>

			<h2>Pokercode</h2>
			<p>The Pokercode bot helps the server staff manage member roles. To do so, it stores:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Role changes</strong>: when a member gains or loses a role, the member's Discord user ID,
					the role ID, whether the role was added or removed, and the date.
					This is used to remove time-limited roles once they expire, to send the scheduled
					role-based messages, and for the staff role reports.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Daily role counts</strong>: once a day, for each tracked role, the number of members
					holding it and the list of their Discord user IDs, used for the staff statistics.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				The bot does not read, store or log the content of any message.
				When a staff member uses the <code>/csv-drop</code> command, the uploaded CSV file of user IDs is only
				processed in memory to give a role to the listed members, and is never stored.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Retention</strong>: role changes and daily role counts are automatically deleted after
				<strong>30 days</strong>.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Security</strong>: the Discord user and role IDs are encrypted (AES-256-GCM) before they are written
				to the database, so they are encrypted at rest. The database dumps sent to backup storage are encrypted as well.
			</p>

			<h2>Pokercode Quiz</h2>
			<p>
				The Pokercode Quiz bot posts poker quizzes. When you answer one, it stores your Discord user ID,
				the quiz you answered, the points you earned and the date. This is used to display the
				lifetime, monthly, weekly and sprint leaderboards and the <code>/rank</code> and <code>/stats</code> commands.
				These answers are kept as long as the leaderboard exists, unless you ask for their deletion.
				The bot does not read, store or log the content of any message.
			</p>

			<h2>What we do not do</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>We do not sell, rent or share your data with third parties.</li>
				<li>We do not use your data for advertising, profiling, or to train machine learning or AI models.</li>
				<li>We do not collect any data outside of the Pokercode Discord server.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Where the data is stored</h2>
			<p>
				The data is stored in a PostgreSQL database on servers operated by Simon Lefort, with backups on
				OVHcloud object storage. Only the bots and their maintainer can access it.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				You can ask for a copy of the data stored about you, or for its deletion, at any time by emailing
				<a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> with your Discord user ID.
				Requests are handled within 30 days.
				Leaving the Pokercode server stops any new data collection about you.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page is updated.
				Questions: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
			</p>
		</article>
	</div>
</Layout>
